<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leeward Islands (Society Islands)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Îles Sous-le-Vent, Leeward Society Islands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> are the western group of the Society Islands in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, including Raiatea, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huahine">Huahine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bora-bora">Bora Bora</a>. Their chiefdoms stayed independent of the Kingdom of Tahiti, and an Anglo-French declaration of 1847 guaranteed their independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed them in 1888, but resistance on Raiatea lasted until 1897.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leeward-islands-society-islands.jpg" alt="Leeward Islands (Society Islands)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VateGV · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Leeward_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
